tel 1.0

# An example presentation, which `fuel present doc/slides.tel` shows in a browser: a slide holds
# Markdown or a block of code, and consecutive slides of code in one language are animated from
# one to the next. A slide's `syntax` names its code's language, and may say what a fence's
# preamble says — marks, `context`, `errors`, frames — with the code itself beneath `code`, and
# a `label` for its frame. A slide's `transcript` is what is said while it is shown, which
# `fuel transcript doc/slides.tel` prints in order.
title  Fuel, in three slides of code

slide
  markdown
      # Fuel, in three slides of code

      Each code slide below is a frame of one animation: step with the arrow keys, and press
      `f` for full screen.
  transcript
      Welcome. Fuel can show a presentation in a browser, and this one has three slides of
      code, each a frame of one animation.

slide
  syntax scala
      val greeting: Text = t"Hello"
  transcript
      We start with a greeting.

slide
  syntax scala
    label  a new value, from the first
    highlight shouted  derived
    code
        val greeting: Text = t"Hello"
        val shouted: Text = greeting.upper

slide
  syntax scala
    label  and its size
    highlight size
    code
        val greeting: Text = t"Hello"
        val shouted: Text = greeting.upper
        val size: Int = shouted.length

slide
  markdown
      That's all.
  transcript
      And that is all.
